<statement>
<p>
	This program provides a visual version of the current state of the Tic-Tac_Toe game board. The board should be a character array that can be displayed using MATLAB&#x27;s &lt;pf&gt;disp&lt;/pf&gt; command. Your visual game board should contain the available spaces as an absolute index location and the spaces occupied by either X or O. A template board is provided.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>You may want to use your</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>P42</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>program here.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		gameboard = TTT43_display_board_lastname([0 0 0; 0 1 0; 0 0 0])
		disp(' ');disp(gameboard)
		1 | 4 | 7
		-----------
		2 | X | 8
		-----------
		3 | 6 | 9
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
